:: zahara
You spot a lone figure crouched beside a cactus in the blazing sun. There are several other big, beautiful cacti surrounding her.
As you approach, Zahara looks up and says, "Oh, welcome to my cactus garden. I call it "The Factor Patch".

Want to hear a cactus joke?

<<linkreplace [[How unbecoming of you. This is a serious matter!->zahara: cacti]]

'I have no choice, do I?' t8n>>"Nope! Here it is: How did the cactus get an A+ on their test?"

    <<linkreplace 'Umm...I dunno, why?' t8n>>

        "Because they were a really sharp student!"
    
        <<linkreplace 'I didn\'t think a cactus could go to school...' t8n>>

            "Ah. Well, I guess you have a POINT there. But really, there's no need to NEEDLE me about it!"
        
            [[Wait for her to stop lauging.->zahara: cacti]]
        <</linkreplace>>
    <</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>

:: zahara: cacti
"I take you came from Bloom School? That gardener told you where I was, didn't he?
Well, as long as you're here, I could use some help with my cacti.
They're actually 'Cactori'...Factor cacti. They can only grow with the power of factors.
Can you pick a cactus and guide the factor tree until it blooms?

[[Ask how it works.->zahara: lesson]]
